# OKF

Three names, three jobs:

| Name | Job |
| --- | --- |
| **OKF** | The format: inert Markdown records with YAML frontmatter, collections, and links. |
| **`okf` crate** | Portable engine: parse, validate, graph, search, artifacts. No HTML or desktop. |
| **`okmate`** | The application: CLI, Askama preview, desktop window. Depends on `okf` only. |

The crate README is
[okf/README.md](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/blob/main/okf/README.md).

## Profiles

`Profile::Base` is portable OKF. `Profile::Strict` adds owners and evidence.
This repository's knowledge tree uses `--profile strict`.

## Artifacts

`okmate build` writes `catalog.json`, `search.json`, `validation.json`,
`llms.txt`, and Askama HTML for **one bundle**. That `llms.txt` is not this
site's `/llms.txt`. The product-site index is generated by Rocdown from page
titles and descriptions.

## What okmate does not do

`okmate` does not compile Rocdown. `rocdown` refuses OKF records and points
here. Keep project knowledge in `knowledge/` and product pages in `site/`.
